A casino table pays a certain ratio if you get a blackjack with your first 2 cards. If you scored a blackjack and were paid $60 with an original bet of $40, what is the payout ratio for getting a blackjack?
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The payout ratio is the ratio of the amount you receive on a game to the amount you should pay to get the game. In this case, the ratio is the amount you received divided by the actual amount you paid.

The ratio is calculated as follows:

\[
\text{Profit} = \text{Amount you received} - \text{Original bill} = 60 - 40 = 20
\]

\[
\text{Profit Ratio} = \frac{\text{Amount you received}}{\text{Original bill}} = \frac{60}{40} = 1.5
\]

Thus, the proportion is $\boxed{1.5:1}$ .
