","To prove that the Riemann-Lapyowski fractional differential operators \( aD_t^p \) and \( aD_t^q \) do not commute in general, we proceed as follows:

1. **Definition of the Riemann-Lapavyowski fractional differential operators**:
   The fractional differential operator \( aD_t^p \) is defined as:
   \[
   aD_t^p f(t) = \int_{0}^{t} a(t - t_0) \left( \frac{1}{t_0} \right)^p f(t_0) \, dt_0.
   \]
   The general form is:
   \[
   aD_t^p f(t) = \int_{0}^{t} a(t - t_0) \left( \frac{t - t_0}{t_0} \right)^{p-1} f(t_0) \, dt_0.
   \]
   Here, \( p \) is the order of the fractional derivative, and \( a(t) \) is the weight function.

2. **Compute \( aD_t^p (aD_t^q f(t)) \)**:
   \[
   aD_t^p (aD_t^q f(t)) = \int_{0}^{t} a(t - t_0) \left( \frac{t - t_0}{t_0} \right)^{p-1} \left( \int_{0}^{t_0} a(t_0 - t_1) \left( \frac{t_0 - t_1}{t_1} \right)^{p-1} f(t_1) \, dt_1 \right) \, dt_0.
   \]

