","The square wave-mass is defined as the difference between the difference in four-momicsics:  
\[
Q^2 = (p_f - p_i)^2
\]  
Substituting the four-momentum vectors:  
\[
Q^2 = (E_f/c - E_i/c, \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i)^2
\]  
Expanding the dot product:  
\[
Q^2 = \left( \frac{E_f}{c} - \frac{E_i}{c} \right)^2 - \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right) \cdot \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf_i \right)
\]  
Simplify the first term:  
\[
Q^2 = \left( \frac{E_f - E_i}{c} \right)^2 - \left( \mathbf{p}_f \cdot \mathbf{p}_f - 2 \mathbf{p}_f \cdot \mathbf{p}_i + \mathbf{p}_i \cdot \mathbf{p}_i \right)
\]  
