In a Cartesian coordinate system, what is the curl of a vector field \(\mathbf{V}(x, y)\) that depends only on \(x\) and \(y\)? Express the result in terms of its components.<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","To compute the curl of a vector field \(\mathbf{V}(x, y)\) in a Cartesian coordinate system, we use the formula:

\[
\mathbf{V}(x, y) = \mathbf{i} f(x, y) + \mathbf{j} g(x, y).
\]

The curl is given by:

\[
\mathbf{curl} \, \mathbf{V} = \nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \mathbf{k} \left( \frac{\partial f}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial g}{\partial x} \right).
